      "function": "flb_utils_write_str",
      "line": null,
      "code": "len = snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp) - 1, \"\\\\u%04x\", codepoint);",
      "note": "Root cause. On the exact crashing key, byte 15 `0xf2` reaches `const char *str` without unsigned normalization, so `uint32_t c = (uint32_t) str[i];` sign-extends it to `0xfffffff2` and the call takes the `c > 0xFFFF` branch. `flb_utf8_decode()` still resolves bytes `f2 88 88 88` to `0x88208`, so this `snprintf` returns 7 for `\\\\u88208` after only a 6-byte availability check. The patch adds `if ((available - written) < len) return FLB_FALSE;` immediately after this line and duplicates the same obligation at the sibling `\\\\u%.4x` and `\\\\u%.4hhx` escape sites.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
